    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "1. Can I Chew Gum While Wearing Invisalign Aligners Daily? No. Remove your aligners before chewing gum. Gum can stick to the trays, cause bacteria buildup, and prevent them from fitting snugly during your Invisalign journey. 2. I Enjoy Chewing Gum. Is Sugar-free Gum Safe With Invisalign? Yes, but only after removing your aligners. Sugar-free gum with xylitol helps reduce bacteria buildup, but chewing with aligners can damage them and affect your treatment progress. Always brush before placing the aligners back. 3. What Should I Do if I Accidentally Chew Gum While Wearing Invisalign? Gum can distort the clear plastic and make the trays not fit snugly. If this happens, contact your orthodontist or dentist to check the aligners and protect your Invisalign treatment. 4. Do Artificial Sweeteners in Gum Affect Invisalign Aligners? Artificial sweeteners do not directly harm the trays, but chewing gum with aligners in can trap saliva and increase bacteria buildup. Remove aligners daily before chewing anything except water. 5. Can I Feel Confident Wearing Invisalign if I Quit Chewing Gum? Yes. Invisalign aligners are clear, BPA-free, and discreet so that you can feel confident without gum. If you enjoy chewing gum, remove the trays first, brush your teeth, rinse with lukewarm water, and avoid hot water to protect them."
    }
